Notes on Recode File

1    There are 21 households in which there are no dejure adult members,
     including 15 households in which there are no dejure memmbers.

2.   There is 1 household in which the head of the household is not the first
     member listed in the household listing, but the second.

3.   There is one case in which HV216 (rooms for sleeping) was corrected from
     "00" to missing.

4.   There are 717 cases in which the field supervisor reported in the
     individual questionnaire is not the same as that reported in the
     household.

5.   There are 93 cases in which the field editor reported in the individual
     questionnaire is not the same as that reported in the household.

6.   There are 6 cases in which the office editor reported in the individual
     questionnaire is not the same as that reported in the household.

7.   There are 46 cases in which the respondent's report of current school
     enrollment is different from that reported in the household.

8.   There is 1 case in which it is not possible to classify the respondent
     regarding literacy (V108 = missing), but the respondent reports reading a
     newspaper (V109 = 1).

9.   There are 24 births for which the age at death was reported as 1 year.

10.  There are 2 cases in which the woman reported ever use of male
     sterilization, but is not currently using male sterilization.

11.  There is 1 case in which the mother is currently breastfeeding because of
     the penultimate child's being breastfed while the last birth is not being
     breastfed.

12.  There is birth case in which M4 is missing and M34 is blank because the
     response to the question regarding ever breastfed is missing.

13.  There is 1 child with a vaccination card, but no vaccinations given.

14.  There is 1 case in which the woman's reported age at marriage is 8 years.

15.  There are 116 cases in which the woman's reported age for her spouse is
     two or more years different from that reported in the household.

16.  Country specific variable S610 includes all responses to question 610,
     while V376 includes the response of only those women not intending to use
     in the future.

17.  There are 5 cases in which V801 = 0 minutes there are 37 cases in which
     V801 is greater than 180 minutes.

18.  MM14 is applicable for only those women who died from complications due to
     pregnancy or delivery.

19.  Country specific variable S903 contains the originally reported number of
     siblings born before the respondent.  Due to inconsistencies related to
     the constructed century month code of births, the corrected number of
     siblings born before the respondents is reported in MMC2.

Notes on couples (linking the male and female recode files)

In linking the couples that can be found in the women's and men's recode files,
there are some mismatches.  Only couples for which there is consistency in
reporting should be used for analysis.

1.   There are 46 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is not in the men's recode file because he was not eligible.

2.   There are 26 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is in the men's recode file, but he does not have a complete
     questionnaire.

3.   There are 6 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is in the men's recode file, but he does not report the woman
     as his wife in his variable MV034.

4.   There are 107 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's
     recode file is not in the women's recode file because she was not
     eligible.

5.   There are 14 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's recode
     file is in the women's recode file, but she does not have a complete
     questionnaire.

6.   There are 8 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's recode
     file is in the women's recode file, but she does not report the man as her
     husband in her variable V034.

Inconsistencies in the Data File

1.   There are 2 cases in which V215 exceeds the interval since the last birth;
     both are flagged.

2.   There is 1 case in which V215 = 96 (never menstruated), but the woman has
     given birth.

3.   There are 85 children for whom a date of vaccination is less than 7 days
     after a previous vaccination.

4.   There are 328 children who are less than 24 months of age but for whom
     HW15 = 2 (measured standing); there are 162 children 24 months of age or
     greater for whom HW15 = 1 (measured lying down).

5.   There are 7 children whose BCG scar was reported as seen (HW14 = 1), but
     for whom H2 equals 0; there are 317 children whose BCG scar was reported
     as not seen (HW14 = 0), but H2 equal 1.

6.   There are 3 cases for whom V525 (sexual experience) = 0, but they report
     being married.

7.   There are 25 cases in which V502 = 0 (never married), but V630A = 1.

8.   There are 64 cases in which V212 (age at first birth) is less than V525
     (age at first sexual experience); all cases are flagged.

9.   V867 is constructed from two questions.  The original responses have been
     placed in country specific variables S821A and S821B.

10.  In the maternal mortality section, there are 34 cases for which an
     inconsistency was found between the reported number of births prior to the
     respondent's birth and the century month codes of birth that have been
     imputed.  The originally reported number of births is stored in country
     specific variable S903; the "corrected" number of births is stored in
     MM2C.

Coding Additions

1.   The range for V154 has been extended to include the code "11", labelled
     "No birth certificate".

2.   The range for V375A has been extended to include the code "95", labelled
     "No reason given".

