Notes on Male Recode File

1.   There are 398 cases in which the field supervisor reported in the
     individual questionnaire is not the same as that reported in the
     household.

2.   There are 40 cases in which the field editor reported in the individual
     questionnaire is not the same as that reported in the household.

3.   There are 16 cases in which the respondent's report of current school
     enrollment is different from that reported in the household.

4.   There are 6 cases in which the age of the wife reported in MV034 is
     reported in the household as less than 15.

5.   There are 25 cases in which the man reported ever use of female
     sterilization but is not currently using it.

6.   There are 5 cases in which the age at marriage is less than 12; 3 reported
     information for marriage at 11; 2 reported marriage at 10.

7.   There is one case in which MV801 = 0 minutes; there is one case in which
     MV801 is greater than 180 minutes.
8.   MV867 is constructed from two questions.  The original responses have been
     placed in country specific variables S523A and S523B.

9.   MV213, MV610 and MV621 are applicable only for men for whom MV502 = 1 (in
     union) or MV534 = 1 (has a regular partner).

Notes on couples (linking the male and female recode files)

In linking the couples that can be found in the women's and men's recode files,
there are some mismatches.  Only couples for which there is consistency in
reporting should be used for analysis.

1.   There are 46 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is not in the men's recode file because he was not eligible.

2.   There are 26 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is in the men's recode file, but he does not have a complete
     questionnaire.

3.   There are 6 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of the women's
     recode file is in the men's recode file, but he does not report the woman
     as his wife in his variable MV034.

4.   There are 107 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's
     recode file is not in the women's recode file because she was not
     eligible.

5.   There are 14 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's recode
     file is in the women's recode file, but she does not have a complete
     questionnaire.

6.   There are 8 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the men's recode
     file is in the women's recode file, but she does not report the man as her
     husband in her variable V034.

Inconsistencies in the Male Data File

1.   There is 1 case for whom MV525 (sexual experience) = 0, but he reports
     being married.

2.   There is 1 case for which MV613 = 10, but MV625 = 5 and MV628 and MV629
     equal 96.

3.   There is 1 case for which MV602 = 4 MV616 = 998.  All men are asked if
     they would like additional children, even those men who have been
     sterilized.  The woman's recode excludes sterilized women from that
     question.

